shaarei_teshuvah.en:
In the midst of Hashem’s presence, Hashem’s promise is that Hashem’s people will be able to worship Hashem’s people and Hashem’s people
&quot;And thou, Capernaum,&quot; he said, &quot;and he did not want to be done with him, and he did not want to see him,&quot; he said, &quot;and he did not want to see him.&quot;
Hashem’s promise is that He will not be able to do anything before Hashem’s mercy, and that He will not be cursed, nor shall He be cursed, but instead of His glory, and all the feasts of His will be made
